# Identity consolidation for release notes and `git shortlog`.
#
# One person committing from two addresses is credited once. Nothing here
# changes history; git applies it at read time, and `git log --use-mailmap` is
# what pkg/relnotes reads.
#
# Format:  Canonical Name <canonical@email>  Other Name <other@email>
#
# The addresses in this file are the ones already in every commit's author and
# Signed-off-by trailer. They are here because git needs them to tell two people
# apart, and they never reach release notes — pkg/relnotes.CheckNoEmails fails
# the build if one does.
#
# If you would rather not be credited at all, see docs/oss/no-credit.md. No
# reason is required.

Luke Greene <luke.greene86@gmail.com>
Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
